course: dictionary
lesson: 7063
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The rest of the sentence tells you which one the writer means. «The vicar led everyone in saying the Paternoster before the service.» The vicar and the service show that Paternoster means a prayer, the Lord's Prayer.
explain: The same word can name a lift. «Step onto the paternoster, and it carries you slowly up to the top floor.» Step onto, carries and floor are your clues: this paternoster is a lift, not a prayer.
explain: Ask yourself: what is the sentence about? Then try each meaning in place of the hard word and see which one still makes sense. If you are unsure, check the dictionary.
fact: A paternoster is a noun, so it names a thing or a prayer.
fact: «Paternoster» means the Lord's Prayer, the prayer Jesus taught.
fact: The name comes from its first words in Latin, «Pater noster», meaning «Our Father».
fact: In church, a paternoster can also be one bead in a rosary, or a whole string of prayer beads.
fact: In the UK, a paternoster lift is an old kind of lift made of open cabins that keep moving slowly in a loop: «A paternoster is an old kind of lift that never stops: open cabins go round in a loop and people step on and off as a cabin slowly passes.»
exercise: «The vicar led everyone in saying the Paternoster before the service.» What does Paternoster mean here? | A lift in a tall shop | *The Lord's Prayer | A kind of sweet bread | A string of prayer beads
exercise: «Grandma's paternoster beads clicked as she prayed.» What is a paternoster in this sentence? | The Latin words for Our Father | *One bead, or a string of prayer beads | A type of bird | A lift with open cabins
exercise: «Step onto the paternoster, and it carries you slowly up to the top floor.» Which meaning fits? | A window on the top floor | The Lord's Prayer | *An old lift of open cabins that moves in a loop | A string of prayer beads
test: «The paternoster in the old office block never stops, so people step on and off as it passes.» Which clue shows that paternoster means a lift? | office block | the | never | *step on and off
test: The Latin words «Pater noster» mean what in English? | Our Lord | Our Kingdom | Our Bread | *Our Father
exam: A child reads «She held her paternoster tightly as she prayed.» What does paternoster mean? | A kind of bread | A lift | *A string of prayer beads | A bird
